# Vendored upstream IPTC Sport Schema 1.1 bytes.
#
# These files are a byte-exact copy of https://github.com/iptc/sport-schema at the
# pinned commit, and their sha256 is asserted by
# agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/upstream-commit.json
# on every harness run. Upstream ships trailing whitespace throughout, so Git's
# whitespace checks would flag every line — and "fixing" it would break the pin,
# void the licence notice's "no changes were made" statement, and invalidate every
# conformance result measured against these bytes.
#
# So: mark them vendored, and turn off diff and whitespace checking for them ONLY.
# Nothing else in the repository is affected, and reviewability is preserved for
# everything Machina actually authored.

agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/ontologies/** linguist-vendored -diff -whitespace
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/shacl/** linguist-vendored -diff -whitespace
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/vocabularies/** linguist-vendored -diff -whitespace
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/samples/** linguist-vendored -diff -whitespace
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/tools/** linguist-vendored -diff -whitespace
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/README.md linguist-vendored -diff -whitespace
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/credits.markdown linguist-vendored -diff -whitespace

# One baseline fixture is a byte-exact copy of a pre-existing checked-in example
# (agent-templates/iptc-mappings/example-iptc-event.json), whose EOF blank line is
# part of those bytes. PR 1 is output-neutral, so the example is not rewritten to
# suit the copy, and the copy is not altered to suit Git — provenance.json claims a
# verbatim copy and that claim stays literally true.
#
# So: turn off whitespace checking for this ONE file. It stays fully diffable and
# is NOT marked vendored: it is a Machina-authored fixture and is reviewed as one.
tools/iptc/fixtures/baseline/api-football-soccer-event-nulls.json -whitespace

# The official Creative Commons CC BY 4.0 legal code, published verbatim in this
# distribution because `pyproject.toml` names it in `license-files`. Creative
# Commons ends the text with a blank line, so Git's whitespace check reports
# `new blank line at EOF` and a pre-commit hook refuses the file. Trimming that
# byte would satisfy the hook and stop this being the CC BY 4.0 legal code — it
# would break the pinned sha256 the package proof asserts, and a licence this
# repository edited is not the licence it names in `License-Expression`.
#
# So: same treatment as the pinned upstream ontologies above, for this ONE file.
# `LICENSES/MIT.txt` and `NOTICE-IPTC.md` are Machina-authored and stay fully
# reviewed — no glob here may widen over them.
LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt linguist-vendored -diff -whitespace

# Machina-authored, and therefore deliberately NOT vendored: these are reviewed
# like any other file in the repository, with diff and whitespace checks on. They
# are the three files upstream-commit.json does not hash, and the same three names
# that tools/iptc/reference.py exempts from its unmanifested-file check.
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/LICENSE.md !linguist-vendored diff whitespace
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/UPSTREAM.md !linguist-vendored diff whitespace
agent-templates/iptc-mappings/references/iptc-sport-schema-1.1/upstream-commit.json !linguist-vendored diff whitespace
